// VARIANT ROTATION THIS ROUND, decided in .claude/brand-spec-meesub168.md §3 and
// NOT re-picked here: Announcement4 replaces Announcement5, LatestWinners3 replaces
// LatestWinners2, Faq (the BASE file) replaces Faq4, ReviewCardSumo2 replaces the base
// ReviewCardSumo, and the ContentBox shape-mix drops FloatingBadge / Neumorphism /
// TwoPremium / the base SevenThree / SevenThreePremium / TwoCyberCut / 3ThreePremium for
// Premium / CyberCut / TwoNeumorphism / SevenThreeNeumorphism / SevenThreeFloatingBadge /
// Special / the base 3Three — **zero overlap with the outgoing brand's mix**.
// NavbarStyle3 + FooterStyle3 are the layout's pair this round and the brand font moves
// google-sans -> kanit; all of that is the orchestrator's shared-chrome step, not this
// page's.
// ⚠️ ContentBox.astro (the base) is NOT in this round's index mix — it is still always-live
// shared chrome, because terms, privacy, 404, /promotion and the button pages all render
// through it, so the orchestrator rethemes it and **this page neither uses nor edits it**.
// An "is it used?" check has to match the bare filename rather than the components/ path,
// which is how a component reached only from another file got misread as inventory once.
// Every unused *Style / *Premium / *Cyber / *Huay / *CyberCut / *FloatingBadge sibling,
// the other Faq* and Announcement* files, the other LatestWinners* and the base
// ReviewCardSumo all stay on disk as inventory for the next brand — nothing was deleted,
// and the earlier brands' hues still inside them are expected drift.
//
// Eight widgets this template usually offers are deliberately absent, and they are named
// without their file extension on purpose because the playbook's "is this component live?"
// check is a bare-filename grep: ProviderGrid and ProviderGridPremium are banned by
// brand-spec §6 because this brief names NO game studio and NO bank at all,
// GameRankingBoard has no ranking to carry, SmoothCarousel has no brief section asking for
// a carousel, LoginRtpSection is out because its RTP table would put an RTP figure on the
// page while §6 allows only the brief's own three numbers (0.3%, 0.8%, 24ชม.),
// FeaturedGames / PopularGamesStrip / LottoGrid would all have to invent game names the
// brief never writes, and FeatureHighlights is out because **this brief has no sub-list
// under any heading** — the previous brand's brief had "ขั้นตอนที่ 1-3", this one does not,
// so there is nothing for it to render and the page's h3 count stays at the brief's own two.
//
// <Announcement /> runs bare on purpose: Announcement4's default message is this brand's
// copy, written from this brief by the orchestrator, and every sub-page calls it bare too —
// so passing an override here is exactly how the ticker ends up saying two different things
// on two pages of the same site.
